<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Education Payroll</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Specialised salary processing for schools, colleges, and educational institutions: <strong>permanent teaching staff</strong> (pay commission/institutional scales), <strong>contractual teachers</strong>, <strong>visiting/part-time faculty</strong> (honorarium with TDS S.194J), <strong>non-teaching admin</strong>, and <strong>support workers</strong> (transport, canteen, security). Must align with <strong>academic calendars, pay commissions, MEPS Act, RTE Act, UGC/AICTE norms</strong>, and trust/society accounting.</p><p>Salary varies enormously within one institution: UGC professor Rs 2L+/month vs peon at min wages. Visiting faculty = not employees (194J, not 192). Academic calendar: summer vacation salary, exam duty, June/July increments. Most Mumbai schools are <strong>trust/society-run</strong> = dual compliance: payroll under labour laws AND trust accounts under <strong>Maharashtra Public Trusts Act 1950</strong> with Charity Commissioner. <strong>RTE Act 2009</strong> mandates teacher qualifications and student-teacher ratios with financial implications.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Education Payroll in Mumbai:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>MEPS Act 1977:</strong> Maharashtra private school teacher service conditions. Pay scales, leave, PF, gratuity, retirement age, disciplinary procedure.</p><p><strong>UGC/AICTE 7th CPC:</strong> College faculty scales. Professor Level 14, Assoc Prof 13A, Asst Prof Level 10 + AGP. DA revised periodically. HRA per city (Mumbai = X).</p><p><strong>Visiting Faculty S.194J:</strong> Honoraria = professional fees. TDS 10%. Form 16A (not 16). No PF/ESI. Threshold: Rs 30K/year per faculty.</p><p><strong>Academic Calendar Payroll:</strong> Summer vacation salary (permanent). Pro-rata mid-term. Exam duty payments. Increments June/July (not April).</p><p><strong>Trust IX-C:</strong> Payroll expenditure in trust accounts for Charity Commissioner. Salary from designated trust accounts. 12A/80G 85% application rule.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
