                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is PF and ESI mandatory for school and college staff?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. PF for 20+ employees (teaching + non-teaching combined), 12%+12% on Basic+DA. ESI for 10+ employees, wages ≤ Rs 21,000 - covers most non-teaching + junior staff. Even trust-run schools are covered. Remitted by 15th monthly. Patron handles registration and filing with EPFO/ESIC Mumbai.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much does education payroll cost in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Pre-school: Rs 5,000-10,000/month. Small school (20-50 staff): Rs 10,000-20,000. Medium school/junior college (50-150): Rs 20,000-40,000. Degree/engineering college (150-500): Rs 35,000-1,00,000. Multi-branch network: Rs 75,000-2,50,000. Coaching/EdTech: Rs 10,000-35,000.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How are teacher salaries different from corporate CTC?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Teacher salaries follow pay scale structures (Basic + Grade Pay/AGP + DA + HRA) prescribed by pay commissions, not employer-designed CTC. Government-aided: 7th CPC. Private Maharashtra: MEPS Act 1977. College: UGC/AICTE. Increments are academic-year-based (June/July), not April. Patron configures per applicable scale.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What pay scales apply to Mumbai college faculty?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>University of Mumbai-affiliated: UGC/AICTE 7th CPC. Assistant Professor Level 10 (Rs 57,700-1,82,400 + AGP). Associate Professor Level 13A (Rs 1,31,400-2,17,100). Professor Level 14 (Rs 1,44,200-2,18,200). DA revised. HRA per Mumbai X category. Aided: government grant. Unaided: own funds.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Do trust-run schools have separate payroll obligations?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Standard obligations (PF, ESI, TDS, PT, gratuity) PLUS trust-specific: payroll in trust accounts for Charity Commissioner IX-C under Maharashtra Public Trusts Act 1950. Salary from designated trust accounts with documentation. 12A/80G: 85% application toward educational objects - salary is primary application.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>School ke teacher ka payroll kaise?</strong> Pay scale ke hisaab (Basic + Grade Pay + DA + HRA). PF 12%+12%, TDS, Maharashtra PT katta hai. Summer vacation mein permanent staff ko salary milti hai. Trust school ka IX-C Charity Commissioner ko file hota hai.</p><p><strong>Visiting faculty ka TDS alag?</strong> Haan - Section 194J ke under 10% TDS. Form 16A milta hai (16 nahi). PF/ESI nahi lagta.</p><p><strong>College mein UGC scale zaroori?</strong> Aided college mein haan - govt grant UGC/AICTE 7th CPC ke hisaab se. Unaided apna rakh sakta hai lekin minimum norms follow karne chahiye.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
